From 5cf36bc9d9b1da807faff0c18dcbbd1fd5a64f39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Geerinck <xavier.geerinck@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:48:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] fix(sandbox): release stops a running command; bound
 Acquire to 60 s

DELETE waited for the sandbox's turn, so it blocked behind a running
exec for as long as that command ran (forever without timeoutMs), and a
driver Acquire that never returned held the turn and the caller forever.

- release is handled before the turn wait, as Deactivate is. It removes
  the target at once and releases the VM in the background.
- The driver calls that run a command (exec, session start, session
  send) use a context that is also cancelled when the target is
  removed. A call whose target was removed while it ran answers with
  the "sandbox lost" error (410 ERR_SANDBOX_LOST), even if the driver
  answered, because its VM is going away.
- Each driver Acquire is bounded by Options.AcquireTimeout, 60 s by
  default. When the bound passes (and not the caller's own deadline)
  the call fails with ResourceExhausted, which the API maps to 429
  ERR_SANDBOX_HOST_FULL: no sandbox now, retry later.

Exec with timeoutMs 0 is unchanged: no daprd-side deadline on the
command itself. The lock order is unchanged; release takes the factory
lock without the turn, as Deactivate does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
